  "notes": "Measured on A321neos (2025), which all carry 'Jet2holidays'. Many 737-800s wear the same paint with 'Jet2.com' titles in red instead (and no slogan); a few older 737s keep the earlier red-tailed Jet2.com scheme. The title's red-to-orange shading is described, not drawn. The belly aft of the blue sweep's start is blue; nothing else is seen from below. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on G-SUNC (side-on, 2025-08-30): the fuselage title sits wholly under the windows (its J's top just below the window bottoms), so it moved down and its cap height is 0.36 (it had run over the windows); 'Jet2' red and 'holidays' orange as parts; lowercase 0.62 of the J; the blue sweep's edge reduced to its two ends. Jet2's 737-800s carry 'Jet2.com' instead and aren't drawn here.",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation (red fin). The blue-and-sunburst scheme appeared in 2011 (on 757s leased from Allegiant, per press reports) and replaced the red-tailed Jet2.com scheme across most of the fleet."
}
